<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arrow Cross Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1935–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arrow Cross Party was a Hungarian fascist and antisemitic party led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferenc-szalasi">Ferenc Szálasi</a>, which grew from his movement founded in 1935. In October 1944 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> installed it in power after Regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy">Miklós Horthy</a> tried to leave the war. Its militias murdered thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and it sent tens of thousands on death marches before its regime collapsed in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arrow-cross-party.jpg" alt="Arrow Cross Party" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Arrow_Cross_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
